          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq01_p02_c1",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Sets up Bayes' ratio using Courier B branch: $\\frac{0.35 \\times 0.70}{0.83} = \\frac{0.245}{0.83}$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq01_p02_c2",
              "type": "A1",
              "text": "Calculates $\\frac{245}{830} = \\frac{49}{166}$ (or $0.295$ to 3 s.f.)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "question_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq02",
      "parts": [
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq02_p01",
          "marks": 2,
          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq02_p01_c1",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Identifies sampling without replacement with total counters $n + 5$ and writes product $\\frac{5}{n + 5} \\times \\frac{4}{n + 4}$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq02_p01_c2",
              "type": "A1",
              "text": "Simplifies numerator to obtain $\\frac{20}{(n + 5)(n + 4)}$ (or $\\frac{20}{n^2 + 9n + 20}$)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq02_p02",
          "marks": 3,
          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq02_p02_c1",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Equates expression to $\\frac{5}{33}$ and cross-multiplies: $\\frac{20}{(n + 5)(n + 4)} = \\frac{5}{33} \\implies (n + 5)(n + 4) = 132$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq02_p02_c2",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Forms standard 3-term quadratic equation: $n^2 + 9n - 112 = 0$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq02_p02_c3",
              "type": "A1",
              "text": "Factorises $(n - 7)(n + 16) = 0$ and rejects negative root to obtain $n = 7$ blue counters."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "question_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq03",
      "parts": [
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq03_p01",
          "marks": 2,
          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq03_p01_c1",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Expresses Line 3 proportion as $1 - 0.40 - p = 0.60 - p$ and sets up defective equation: $0.02p + 0.40(0.05) + (0.60 - p)(0.04) = 0.038$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq03_p01_c2",
              "type": "A1",
              "text": "Simplifies $0.044 - 0.02p = 0.038 \\implies 0.02p = 0.006$ to obtain $p = 0.30$ (or $\\frac{3}{10}$)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq03_p02",
          "marks": 3,
          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq03_p02_c1",
              "type": "B1",
              "text": "Evaluates Line 3 proportion $0.60 - 0.30 = 0.30$ and joint defective probability $0.30 \\times 0.04 = 0.012$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq03_p02_c2",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Applies Bayes' theorem with total defective probability: $\\frac{0.012}{0.038}$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq03_p02_c3",
              "type": "A1",
              "text": "Simplifies ratio to $\\frac{12}{38} = \\frac{6}{19}$ (or $0.316$ to 3 s.f.)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "question_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq04",
      "parts": [
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq04_p01",
          "marks": 3,
          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq04_p01_c1",
              "type": "B1",
              "text": "Identifies that a score of 2 requires $(1, 1)$, setting $p^2 = \\frac{1}{16}$ and deducing $p = \\frac{1}{4}$ (rejecting $p < 0$)."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq04_p01_c2",
              "type": "B1",
              "text": "Identifies that a score of 6 requires $(3, 3)$, setting $r^2 = \\frac{1}{9}$ and deducing $r = \\frac{1}{3}$ (rejecting $r < 0$)."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq04_p01_c3",
              "type": "A1",
              "text": "Uses $p + q + r = 1$ to obtain $q = 1 - \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{5}{12}$ with full working shown."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq04_p02",
          "marks": 3,
          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq04_p02_c1",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Identifies all pairs summing to 4: $(1, 3)$, $(2, 2)$, and $(3, 1)$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq04_p02_c2",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Substitutes parameter values into sum of products: $2pr + q^2 = 2\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right) + \\left(\\frac{5}{12}\\right)^2$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq04_p02_c3",
              "type": "A1",
              "text": "Calculates $\\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{25}{144} = \\frac{24 + 25}{144} = \\frac{49}{144}$ (or $0.340$ to 3 s.f.)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "question_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq05",
      "parts": [
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq05_p01",
          "marks": 3,
          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq05_p01_c1",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Computes $P(\\text{both red} \\mid \\text{Bag 1}) = \\frac{5}{10} \\times \\frac{4}{9} = \\frac{2}{9}$ and sets up total probability equation: $\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{2}{9}\\right) + \\frac{1}{2} P(\\text{both red} \\mid \\text{Bag 2}) = \\frac{5}{18}$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq05_p01_c2",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Finds $P(\\text{both red} \\mid \\text{Bag 2}) = \\frac{1}{3}$ and equates to $\\frac{x(x - 1)}{(x + 4)(x + 3)}$, cross-multiplying to form $3(x^2 - x) = x^2 + 7x + 12$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq05_p01_c3",
              "type": "A1",
              "text": "Obtains $2x^2 - 10x - 12 = 0 \\implies x^2 - 5x - 6 = 0$ and factorises $(x - 6)(x + 1) = 0$ to deduce $x = 6$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq05_p02",
          "marks": 3,
          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq05_p02_c1",
              "type": "B1",
              "text": "Evaluates favorable joint probability: $P(\\text{Bag 2} \\cap \\text{both red}) = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{1}{6}$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq05_p02_c2",
              "type": "M1",
              "text": "Applies Bayes' theorem: $\\frac{1/6}{5/18}$."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq05_p02_c3",
              "type": "A1",
              "text": "Simplifies to $\\frac{3}{5} = 0.6$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "question_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq06",
      "parts": [
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_probability_m03_l04_cpq06_p01",
          "marks": 2,
